---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About | Custom Lip Cosmetics Manufacturer — MLM Lip"
  description="MLM Lip is the custom lip cosmetics line of Beautychain Limited — GMPC, ISO and CPNP certified manufacturing of private label lip products for brands in North America and Europe."
>
  <section>
    <div class="wrap">
      <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'About' }]} />
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1>The factory behind your lip brand</h1>
      <p class="lead" style="max-width:660px">
        MLM Lip is the lip cosmetics line of {site.manufacturer}, based in Shenzhen, China.
        We work with private label brand owners in North America and Europe — online sellers,
        offline retailers and founders alike — who want their own product, made their way.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="tint">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Why brands pick us</p>
      <h2>What a lip specialist gives you that a generalist factory cannot</h2>
      <div class="grid two" style="margin-top:28px">
        <div class="card">
          <h3 style="font-size:19px;">One roof, not three vendors</h3>
          <p style="margin:0;">Most private label projects fall apart at the seams: the formula lab, the tube supplier and the decorator are separate companies, and nobody owns the mismatch. We run formulation, filling, assembly and decoration under one GMPC-certified roof — the sample you approve is the product you receive.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3 style="font-size:19px;">500 pcs is a principle, not a promo</h3>
          <p style="margin:0;">A 20,000 pcs minimum is not a business decision a new brand can make. We engineered our production line to run profitably at {site.moq} so your first run can be tested in the real market before you scale — not committed before a customer touches it.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3 style="font-size:19px;">Lip is all we do</h3>
          <p style="margin:0;">A factory that makes everything makes nothing well. We concentrate on the six lip formats — gloss, mud, liner, lipstick, oil and mask — which means deeper formulation library, faster shade matching, and packaging components actually stocked for lip work. Body oils and companions are available, but lip is the craft.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3 style="font-size:19px;">Compliance, not paperwork panic</h3>
          <p style="margin:0;">Your first container held at customs over a missing CPSR is a founder's nightmare. Because we operate GMPC and ISO 22716 as standard, the technical dossier your safety assessor and customs broker need is produced as a matter of routine — not scrambled together when the ship has already sailed.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Factory capabilities</p>
      <h2>What our floor can do</h2>
      <div class="grid three" style="margin-top:28px">
        <div class="card gold-line">
          <h3 style="font-size:18px;">Formulation</h3>
          <ul style="margin:0; padding-left:18px; color:var(--ink-soft); line-height:1.8; font-size:14px;">
            <li>Custom shade development & Pantone matching</li>
            <li>Texture tuning (gloss, mud, oil, balm)</li>
            <li>Active-infused formulas (peptides, ceramides)</li>
            <li>Flavor & fragrance systems</li>
            <li>Stability & challenge testing in-house</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="card gold-line">
          <h3 style="font-size:18px;">Packaging & tooling</h3>
          <ul style="margin:0; padding-left:18px; color:var(--ink-soft); line-height:1.8; font-size:14px;">
            <li>200+ library components (tubes, caps, applicators)</li>
            <li>Custom mold opening for exclusive silhouettes</li>
            <li>Silk-screen, hot-stamp, UV digital print</li>
            <li>Gradient spray & metallic finishes</li>
            <li>Carton & secondary packaging design</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="card gold-line">
          <h3 style="font-size:18px;">Production & QC</h3>
          <ul style="margin:0; padding-left:18px; color:var(--ink-soft); line-height:1.8; font-size:14px;">
            <li>GMPC & ISO 22716 certified cleanroom</li>
            <li>Automated high-speed filling & capping</li>
            <li>Batch-to-batch colorimetric control</li>
            <li>Pre-shipment QC with photo reports</li>
            <li>EU CPNP notification & FDA-ready documentation</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Inside the factory</p>
      <h2>See the floor where your products are made</h2>
      <div class="grid two" style="margin-top:24px">
        <div>
          <div class="case-media video-embed">
            <video src="/factory/factory-production.mp4" controls preload="metadata"></video>
          </div>
          <h3 style="margin-top:12px; font-size:18px">Automated Production Line</h3>
          <p class="note" style="margin:0">High-speed precision filling and capping line.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="case-media video-embed">
            <video src="/factory/factory-cleanroom.mp4" controls preload="metadata"></video>
          </div>
          <h3 style="margin-top:12px; font-size:18px">GMPC Cleanroom Operation</h3>
          <p class="note" style="margin:0">Sterile cosmetic manufacturing environment.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Work with us</h2>
      <p class="lead" style="max-width:600px">
        Whether you have a finished concept or just the beginning of an idea, the first step is the same:
        tell us what you want to launch.
      </p>
      <a class="btn" href="/contact">Contact our team</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
